    "findings": {
      "examine": "Endotracheal tube secured at 21 cm at teeth. Bilateral chest hyperinflation with minimal chest wall deflation between breaths. Expiratory wheeze is faint bilaterally with prolonged expiratory phase. Trachea is midline. Neck veins are distended. Peripheral pulses are weak and thready, synchronous with tachycardia.",
      "cxr": "Endotracheal tube tip 3.5 cm above carina. Marked bilateral hyperinflation with 10 posterior ribs visible and flattened diaphragms. Narrow cardiac silhouette. No pneumothorax, focal consolidation, or pleural effusion."
    },
